---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { email, address, legalName } from "../site.js";

const effective = "November 22, 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — Stonework Risk"
  description="How Stonework Risk collects, uses and protects the information you share with us."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <main class="doc">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Updated {effective}</p>

    <p>
      Stonework Risk is the assumed name of {legalName} ("Stonework Risk," "we," "us").
      This policy explains what information we collect through stoneworkrisk.com and in
      the course of placing insurance, how we use it, and the choices you have.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>What you send us.</strong> When you use our contact form or email us, we
        receive what you provide: typically your name, company, email address, phone
        number and message.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>What we need to place coverage.</strong> If you become a client, we collect
        the information carriers require to quote and issue policies, which may include
        business, financial, property, vehicle, driver, payroll and loss history
        information.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Basic technical data.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting provider
        records standard request data such as IP address, browser type and pages
        visited, for security and reliability. We do not use advertising cookies or
        sell access to visitor data.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To respond to your inquiry and provide the services you ask for.</li>
      <li>To obtain quotes, place, service and renew insurance on your behalf.</li>
      <li>To help with claims and communicate with insurance carriers about your coverage.</li>
      <li>To meet our legal, regulatory and licensing obligations.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we share it</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>We do not sell your personal information.</strong> We share it only as
      needed to serve you: with insurance carriers, wholesale brokers and premium finance
      companies involved in placing your coverage; with service providers who help us run
      the agency (for example, email, hosting, form processing and agency management
      software) under obligations to protect it; and where required by law or by an
      insurance regulator.
    </p>

    <h2>How we protect it</h2>
    <p>
      We use reasonable administrative, technical and physical safeguards appropriate to
      the sensitivity of the information, and limit access to people who need it to
      serve you. As an insurance agency we handle nonpublic personal information in line
      with the Gramm-Leach-Bliley Act and applicable Texas law.
    </p>

    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep client records for as long as needed to service your account and as
      required by insurance record-retention rules. Inquiries that don't become client
      relationships are kept only as long as reasonably useful.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      You may ask to see, correct or delete the personal information we hold about you,
      subject to records we're required to keep. Email
      <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a> and we'll respond within a reasonable time.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>This site is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect their information.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If we change this policy, we'll post the new version here and update the date above.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Stonework Risk<br />
      {address.street}<br />
      {address.city}, {address.state} {address.zip}<br />
      <a href={`mailto:${email}`}>{email}</a>
    </p>

    <p class="back"><a href="/">← Back to stoneworkrisk.com</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>
